From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:29:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: carry replies as structured quotes

The quoted message of a received reply (text, author, id) goes into
gowhatsapp_message and is stashed on the conversation as
"webos-quoted-text", "webos-quoted-from" and "webos-quoted-id", so the
app shows a quote card instead of "> " lines in the body. The quote
strings are freed in gowhatsapp_free_message().

A reply from the app arrives as "webos-reply-to" on the conversation
(the id of the quoted message), is resolved through the message cache
and sent as a quote. Replies always take the text path, so a link-only
reply keeps its quote.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
